<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n370" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαυός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> almost always of kings or heroes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>illustrious, noble,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήρυκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.268
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περσεφόνεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.213
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπῆες</span>
			<i>noble</i> guides, <i><span class="en">
				13.71
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.72
			</span></i>; once in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρσαις ἀγαυοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					986
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.229
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of things,
				<i>brilliant, glorious,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					442
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρόος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					9.36
				</span></i>
			; esp. of stars, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				71
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				2.14
			</span></i>(
				Sup.
			):—in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
				<u>in CA</u>
				4p.425M.
			</span></i> (Perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span> intens., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαίω,</span> cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.166
			</span></i>.)</div>
